================================================================================
OBSERVATION
================================================================================
O-6  **A DHCP-learned DNS server is queried in preference to a statically configured one.**
     With `ip name-server 192.168.48.9` configured first and 192.168.48.2 subsequently learned
     by the DHCP client, the relay sent its query to .2 and never ARPed for, let alone queried,
     .9 — while a control with .9 as the only server proves .9 is reachable and used. TFS
     S1570.1.12 says DHCP-provided servers "are always added last of configured name-server
     list". The measurement shows the externally visible preference; it cannot show the
     internal list order, and `show ip name-server` groups by type so it cannot either. Offered
     as a spec-clarification item: either the list order differs from the spec, or "added last"
     describes storage rather than query order and the spec could say so.
     Evidence: work/order-*.{json,err}, work/ctl2-*, work/dnsorder.sh, work/dnsctl2.sh.

